/a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="0000FF"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>formation of DNA loops</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="480"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Looping can be facilitated by </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="1" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>architectural regulator proteins.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr b="0" i="0" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="480"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="1" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Co-activators</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t> may mediate binding by binding to both activator and RNA polymerase.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="199" name="Google Shape;199;p27"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="304800" y="1295400"/><a:ext cx="8382000" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="A three-part diagram that illustrates the interaction between activators/repressors and RNA polymerase in eukaryotes. Starting from the top is a long, narrow rectangular structure divided into seven segments. From the left, the rectangular structure is labeled 5’, followed by a short blue segment, an orange segment with two light blue balls on top, labeled as activator, a short brown segment, labeled as the architectural regulator binding site, another blue segment, a longer purple segment, labeled as the promoter, and a short yellow segment. The end of the yellow segment is labeled 3’. Below the brown segment, a long diagonal arrow pointing down and left has a yellow oval, labeled as the architectural regulator, to its right. The architectural regulator is introduced into the process, which is illustrated by a short curve pointing into the long arrow. Below the long arrow is the rectangular structure described previously with the same segments, but the structure itself is slightly bent, so that it starts at the top left and curves down to the right. The architectural regulator is now lodged on top of the brown segment (architectural regulator binding site). Below this structure is another long arrow pointing down, labeled as recruitment; this time the arrow is beneath the purple segment. To the right of the arrow, two curves are shown pointing into the process, one on top of the other. The top curve shows Pol II, a tan mass with a handle on its left end, entering the process. The bottom curve entering the arrow shows the introduction of the coactivator, a green ovular structure with a curve at its top right, into the process. Below the arrow is the same rectangular structure as the one described previously (with the bound architectural regulator), but this time, the rectangular structure is bent further to the top right, Pol II is bound over the purple segment, and the coactivator is bound to the right of the two light blue balls, so that its bottom sits on top of Pol II. Between the purple and yellow segments is an arrow that points up and then right to green bold letters that say, &quot;ON.&quot; &#xA;" id="200" name="Google Shape;200;p27"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="5105400" y="1447800"/><a:ext cx="3265487" cy="5248275"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>